WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.940
- We all loved you, obviously,

00:00:01.940 --> 00:00:03.500
when you're a part of a show like "Castle"

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:05.576
that lasts for eight seasons,

00:00:05.576 --> 00:00:09.670
you tend to have a fan
base for life from that.

00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:10.640
So I'm just curious, though,

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:12.640
because you now went
into executive producing

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:15.240
and different roles, like,
behind the scenes, too.

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:17.120
What do you, do you think
you learned anything?

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:19.170
Like, I know that you
were acting on that show

00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:21.510
and I know that that was
kind of what you did there,

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:23.590
but is there something you
think you learned from there

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:24.423
in that eight seasons?

00:00:24.423 --> 00:00:25.410
Were you watching everybody,

00:00:25.410 --> 00:00:27.150
were you wanting to end up doing

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:28.520
what you're doing right now?

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:29.850
- Yeah, that's actually something

00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:33.480
that I do talk about
with people on and off.

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:35.190
It's the idea of there are some actors,

00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:39.970
there are some performers, and
I'm guessing even vocalists,

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:44.970
who, they're exclusively kind
of focused on that world.

00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:49.630
And then there are some
actors who are storytellers

00:00:49.630 --> 00:00:52.040
and who really are curious
about the wider scope

00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:53.550
of how do we put this thing together?

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:56.810
And I've always fallen
under that umbrella.

00:00:56.810 --> 00:00:58.820
So even when we were shooting "Castle",

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:01.150
I was always the one who was
sitting at video village,

00:01:01.150 --> 00:01:03.310
talking with the directors,
talking with the writers,

00:01:03.310 --> 00:01:05.940
talking with producers, asking about why--

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:07.000
- Curious.
- What's the difference.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.270
Yeah, what's the difference
between having a character

00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:11.648
focused up here or a
character focused down there.

00:01:11.648 --> 00:01:14.120
And everybody was so open

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:16.610
and so willing to share
their craft with me,

00:01:16.610 --> 00:01:20.100
from camera operators who let
me run the camera sometimes,

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:24.780
to our set designers, and
architects, and carpenters,

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:27.410
and everybody, you know, like
their doors were open to me.

00:01:27.410 --> 00:01:28.370
And that was such a gift.

00:01:28.370 --> 00:01:30.209
And I ended up getting so much information

00:01:30.209 --> 00:01:32.620
just by sitting there,
just by being there.

00:01:32.620 --> 00:01:34.291
And I didn't realize after eight years

00:01:34.291 --> 00:01:39.140
how much now I'm almost
subconsciously unconsciously capable

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:40.620
of contributing to a story.

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:44.230
And I've reaped the rewards
of a lot of that now,

00:01:44.230 --> 00:01:47.540
in this phase, as an
executive producer on a show.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:48.850
And I'm really, I enjoy it.

00:01:48.850 --> 00:01:51.210
I enjoy contributing to
the story on that level.

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:52.340
- It's just really cool.

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:55.890
It just shows that you're curious
and you're invested in it.

00:01:55.890 --> 00:01:57.840
It shows that in the show that you're,

00:01:57.840 --> 00:01:59.890
that you're that kind of
interested in the story,

00:01:59.890 --> 00:02:01.070
and every part counts.

00:02:01.070 --> 00:02:02.400
That's my favorite part of watching shows,

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:05.400
when you can tell that the
writers or the producers,

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:08.410
like, nobody's like a throw off character.

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:11.120
Everybody is, like, involved
in there and it all counts.

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:12.408
And I think when it all matters,

00:02:12.408 --> 00:02:14.060
those are the best stories.

00:02:14.060 --> 00:02:16.400
So great job, it's an awesome show.

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:17.500
- Thank you very much.

